# =============================================================================
# Config: HPRC v1 chr1 — HG002 noisy reads (L=25)
# =============================================================================
# Query config for find_mems + gafpack against the hprcv1-chr1 index using
# HG002 haplotype-1 reads.
#
# HG002 is OUT-OF-GRAPH for this index (verified: 0 of 2262 paths match
# '^HG002#'), so this exercises MEM finding on sequence the pangenome does
# not contain.
#
# Reads: simulated from the HG002 v1.1 Q100 PATERNAL assembly FASTA
# (hg002v1.1.pat.PanSN.fa.gz, md5-verified against the published checksum),
# contig HG002#1#chr1, wgsim -S 42, wgsim defaults (~2% base error + 0.1% mutations, 15% of which are indels).
# Not graph-extracted, so the contig is unclipped. See
# hprcv1/READS_README.md and hprcv1/reads_work_chr1/generate_hg002_chr1_reads.sh.
#
# Usage:
#   ./query.sh hprcv1-chr1-hg002-noisy-L25.env hprcv1-chr1-2026-08-12 [query-name] [--gaf]
# =============================================================================

# ---- Inputs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# GBZ not needed at query time — included for provenance.
GBZ="$MEM_PROJ/hprcv1-chr1/chr1.gbz"
READS="$MEM_PROJ/hprcv1/chr1.hg002_noisy.reads.txt"

# ---- Naming ---------------------------------------------------------------
BASE="hprcv1_chr1"

# ---- Pipeline parameters --------------------------------------------------
MEM_LEN=25
MIN_OCC=1
VALIDATE_SAMPLE=2000

# ---- Not used at query time -----------------------------------------------
KMER=31
THREADS=64

# ---- Reference run for compare.sh (optional) ------------------------------
REF_DIR=""
REF_BASE=""
